WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.684 --> 00:00:11.784
Every answer an SI system gives you starts as math. Billions of small calculations, all at once.

2
00:00:12.324 --> 00:00:19.544
That math runs on special chips called GPUs. And Nvidia is the world's leading maker of them.

3
00:00:20.415 --> 00:00:23.844
Thousands of these chips, wired together, are used to train a

4
00:00:23.844 --> 00:00:25.984
single frontier model.

5
00:00:26.061 --> 00:00:30.004
So nearly every company at the table is Nvidia's customer, its

6
00:00:30.004 --> 00:00:32.184
partner, or its competitor.

7
00:00:32.537 --> 00:00:40.104
That gives its CEO, Jensen Huang, an unusual position. At the lunch, he sat at the President's side.

8
00:00:40.587 --> 00:00:43.964
According to Semafor, Huang also helped build support for the

9
00:00:43.964 --> 00:00:46.064
accord before the lunch.

10
00:00:46.118 --> 00:00:53.704
Afterwards, he pointed to new chip and computer plants, saying: “it's creating a million jobs here in the United States.”

11
00:00:53.897 --> 00:01:00.344
And his message on safety: “There's no conflict between innovation, technology and safety.”
